   "description": "During the making of Meet The Woo, Vol. 2, there were numerous records that Pop Smoke was \"saving for his album\", with the first song that he KNEW was going to be on it was \"Aim For The Moon,\" (which was originally Travis Scott's record, but Pop recorded with Quavo right after the Travis session). The title of the album was not confirmed before his passing, however the theme came from this song, and was chosen posthumously. This list compiles the songs that Pop Smoke was intending for the album, without a specific order.",
